          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c3_contrastive_learning_opposite_proble",
          "text": "Contrastive learning has the opposite problem: comparing whole series for similarity tends to ignore the fine-grained correlations inside them, and it hinges on augmentations that are notoriously difficult to design for temporal data.",
          "expected_role": "content",
