    {
      "index": 5,
      "id": "method",
      "heading": "Method",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c1_how_timesiam_works_single_time",
          "text": "Here is how TimeSiam works. From a single time series it randomly samples two windows: a past subseries and a current subseries, together called Siamese subseries. The current window is lightly corrupted with a simple augmentation such as masking.",
          "expected_role": "result",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "how",
            "timesiam",
            "works",
            "single",
            "time",
            "series",
            "randomly",
            "samples",
            "two",
            "windows"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c2_two_shared_weight_siamese_encoders_p",
          "text": "Two shared-weight Siamese encoders process the past and current windows, and a decoder with cross-attention reconstructs the masked current series using the past observation as context. That single design choice, reconstructing the current from the past, forces the model to internalize how distant moments in a series relate.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "two",
            "shared-weight",
            "siamese",
            "encoders",
            "process",
            "past",
            "current",
            "windows",
            "decoder",
            "cross-attention"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c3_handle_fact_past_current_windows",
          "text": "To handle the fact that past and current windows can be near or far apart in time, TimeSiam adds learnable lineage embeddings indexed by that relative distance, so one model fluently represents many temporal gaps.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "handle",
            "fact",
            "past",
            "current",
            "windows",
            "near",
            "far",
            "apart",
            "time",
            "timesiam"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c4_objective_simply_squared_reconstruct",
          "text": "The training objective is simply the squared reconstruction error between the true and predicted current series.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
